From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:33:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] policy: derive adaptive capacity from active-chain history

Track connected block-size EMA and local congestion fee recommendations.
Advance the chain-derived estimate only when publishing an active tip; restore
an ancestor's estimate on reorg and reconstruct it at restart. A bounded recent
cache accelerates normal extension and rollback without retaining orphan state.
Local mempool demand affects mining/fee policy, never accepted-block capacity.

eCash block validity remains the configured ABC limit. Block-bearing P2P and
raw disk payload bounds follow current adaptive capacity plus 256 KiB, not the
unused 1 GB ceiling; explicit excessiveblocksize settings remain authoritative.
Development block-index record tag 320401 retains nSize after pruning and reads
legacy conditional-size records. Missing old-pruned/header-only size history
is explicitly unavailable: retain baseline capacity, warn, and require complete
ancestry plus restart for exact reconstruction. Do not infer sizes from headers.

Test real two-node reorg/restart convergence, resource bounds, pruned-index size
retention, cache eviction and conservative unavailable-history behavior. RPC
method-dependent tests belong in the following RPC patch, not this prerequisite.

